<title>CHINA: Giant fish causes traffic jam in Hong Kong.</title>
<headline>Giant fish causes traffic jam in Hong Kong.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>A giant fish caused a traffic jam in Hong Kong when it fell off a truck on the way to a restaurant, local newspapers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Police had to prop up the frozen two-metre (6.5 ft), 100-kg (220 pound) garoupa with a wooden pole as two muscular workers hauled it back on to the truck.</p>
<p>The driver was fined HK$450 (US$58) for failing to secure his goods safely.</p>
